scenario a minute of silence followed by a walk is not a teleport
describe The regression that pins why `hold` calls refresh() and not observe().
describe
describe Re-running the detectors against an observation they have already seen
describe is tempting and wrong: it would re-stamp the epoch that the next real
describe fix is measured from. Under this trace the device is quiet for sixty
describe seconds and then reports a position four hundred metres away — an
describe ordinary walk over the whole interval, and 400 m/s if the interval is
describe taken to have started at the last hold.
describe
describe implausible_speed_mm_s is 55000, so the wrong implementation fires
describe PositionJump here and the right one does not. Nothing else in the
describe fixture distinguishes them.

at 0
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3000
  sats 12 15
  jam none
  spoof none
  motion moving watch
  expect validity valid
  expect trust trusted

at 20000
  hold

at 40000
  hold

at 59000
  hold
  expect validity stale

# 400 m north of the last real fix, sixty seconds after it. One unit of
# latitude here is 1e-7 degrees, which is 11.1 mm, so 400 m is 35932 of them.
# 6.7 m/s — fast for a walk, ordinary for a bicycle, and nowhere near the
# 55 m/s gate. Against the last *hold* it would be 400 m/s.
at 60000
  fix 3d
  pos 5035932 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3000
  sats 12 15
  motion moving watch
  expect validity valid
  expect no-reason position-jump
  expect trust trusted
